<title>FRANCE: Arthuis &quot;satisfied&quot; on France Telecom decision.</title>
<headline>Arthuis &quot;satisfied&quot; on France Telecom decision.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Thursday he was satisfied by the European Union approval of the government's use of funds transferred from France Telecom to lower France's public deficit next year.</p>
<p>&quot;I am very satisfied,&quot; Arthuis told Reuters. &quot;Beyond statistical considerations...the measures that we have taken on structural reforms and on capping public spending will mean that in 1998 we will be under the three percent (of GDP) limit.&quot;</p>
<p>The French government plans to use 37.5 billion francs transferred from France Telecom, in exchange for the assumption of pension liabilities, to cut about 0.5 percent from its 1997 public deficits and help it qualify for entry into the single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe we will be at 2.8 percent in 1998 and in 2001 we will be under the two percent limit,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5071</p>
